{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgVAm5s7F3WAGtGhrYjs6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to carry out the build work for the 11 screens, starting with a check that the component library renders correctly alongside the first screen builds. I start with 01_Splash and 02_Home as the first batch, and I take a screenshot of the library at the same time since that check does not depend on the screens.\n\nFor 01_Splash, the frame is 430 × 932 with a solid #EF2A39 background. The wordmark instance sits at y=210, resized to 171 wide, with every text and vector fill overridden to white. The splash burger image is 220 × 258, centered at y=300, and the tagline sits below it. The status bar sits at (0,0), 430 × 44, with its ink recolored to white, and the home indicator sits at y=898.\n\nFor 02_Home, the layout runs top to bottom: status bar 0–44; header row at y=56 with a 48 × 48 avatar at x=24 and the wordmark at the right; the headline \"Order your favourite\\nfood!\" at y=120 in 30px bold; a search pill plus filter button at y=190; category chips at y=250 (All active, then Combos, Sliders, Classic); then 4 menu cards starting at y=310, each 112 tall with a 12 gap, so the stack ends at 794. The bottom nav sits at y=842 and is 90 tall, reaching 932, and the home indicator overlays it at y=898.\n\nThe four cards use the menu card component with text overrides on Name, Category, Rating and Time, and the thumb fill swapped to the matching media image. The Cheeseburger card takes the Favourite variant so its heart is the filled red one; the other three stay on the default state.\n\nEach screen frame is created at 430 × 932 and placed on a grid: row 1 at y=0 with x at 0, 500, 1000, 1500, 2000, and row 2 at y=1100 with x at 0, 500, 1000, 1500, 2000, 2500. 07_Customize breaks the height rule at 430 × 1140 so its full scroll content is visible: image and copy to 300, portion row at 306, spice selector at 362, toppings header at 460, two rows of 4 tiles at 88 × 104 (548–766), sides header at 780 with 5 tiles at 72 wide in one row (816–920), and a sticky total/Order Now bar at 1040.\n\nFor the product frames 03–06 I keep the same structure and vary the data: Cheeseburger portion 1 at $8.24, 4.9, 26 mins; Veggie portion 1 at $9.99, 4.8, 14 mins; Chicken portion 2 at $12.48, 4.6, 42 mins; Fried Chicken portion 4 at $27.00, 4.7, 38 mins.\n\nThe next things I need are the product screen builds, then 07 plus 08 and 09, then 10 and 11.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5836,"cache_read_input_tokens":108969,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5836,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c4b085e-0924-4a6a-9e18-2faff92322bc","uuid":"88358b9c-4d8e-47eb-986b-3837827b6942","timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:14:12.074Z","thinking_duration_ms":46418}
